From b5474e80d3719084ce19121d462628f1a4b46320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:16:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 37/41] [TSReader] Flush the last segment of a stream as the
 end of the stream

Round 11 finding (Astra): after 041f29f, the segment-end flush of the
seek scan and the clock scan always let the E-AC-3 parser wait for the
next segment. In the last segment of a stream, no next segment comes:
a seek to the last frame of an E-AC-3 stream (also 5.1 without
dependent frames) failed with EOS, and with the only PTS in the last
access unit, a seek anywhere in that segment failed.

AdaptiveStream::IsLastSegment() asks the tree whether a segment follows
the current segment (AdaptiveTree::IsLastSegment, as ensureSegment
does). The segment-end flush passes that value as endOfStream. A live
stream in the last period always has a next segment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
